This repository holds the source, design and written content of sinaida.eu.
It is public so the work can be read. It is not open source, and no license
to use, copy, modify, publish or distribute any part of it is granted.

This applies in particular to the biography, artist statement, project
descriptions and case study texts in src/data/ and src/pages/, and to every
image, video still and photograph in the repository. Those are written and
made by Sinaida Krivchenko.

WHAT IS PERMITTED WITHOUT ASKING

  Reading the code, and learning from it.

  Press and education: journalists, curators, students and researchers may
  reproduce stills and quoted text in articles, reviews, catalogues and
  academic writing, with credit to Sinaida Krivchenko and a link to
  https://sinaida.eu. Advertising is commercial use and is not covered.

THIRD-PARTY CODE AND FONTS

  This repository depends on open source libraries and fonts that keep
  their own licenses. See THIRD-PARTY.md.

THE PROJECTS THEMSELVES

  The artworks documented on this site are licensed individually, and most
  of their source code is open under Apache 2.0. See
